# Single source of truth for the emberian/plonky3-recursion fork rev.
#
# P3_REV is the CI clone rev of the `update-plonky3-rev` fork tip that every
# plonky3-recursion consumer in this repo must pin in LOCKSTEP -- they are the
# SAME circuit or the verifier keys fork:
#   - Cargo.toml                             (root [workspace.dependencies]
#                                             p3-recursion/p3-circuit/... git rev
#                                             -- the AUTHORITATIVE pin)
#   - .github/workflows/extension.yml        (sibling clone REV)
#   - .github/workflows/publish-sdk-ts.yml   (sibling clone REV)
#   - .github/workflows/pages-wasm.yml       (sibling clone REV, all three wasm jobs;
#                                             this was pages.yml until 2026-07-26, when
#                                             the Pages deploy split into a cargo-free
#                                             content path + this heavy wasm workflow)
#   - wasm/Cargo.toml                        (sibling-checkout comment)
#   - circuit-prove/src/recursive_witness_bundle.rs
#                                            (RECURSION_P3_REV -- the proving-
#                                             system id folded into the recursive
#                                             VK hash / trust anchor)
#   - .github/workflows/ci.yml               (⚑ ADDED 2026-08-02: TWO sibling clones --
#                                             the wasm job and the forge-ci-runner job --
#                                             both `[patch]` targets. Unwatched by the gate
#                                             for its whole life despite the job's own
#                                             comment saying they "must stay in lockstep or
#                                             the VK forks". Matched by the `REV=<hex>`
#                                             assignment, NOT a blind 40-hex grep: this file
#                                             also pins MATHLIB_REV at 40 hex, which a blind
#                                             grep would report as fork drift.)
#   - .github/workflows/feature-surface.yml  (⚑ ADDED 2026-08-02: the deos-zed-full shard
#                                             clone, same story, same `REV=` matcher.)
#
# When you bump the fork: change P3_REV here, update every consumer above, then
# run `bash scripts/check-p3-rev.sh` to confirm they all agree.
#
# `scripts/check-p3-rev.sh` reads this value and FAILS if ANY consumer above
# drifts -- including RECURSION_P3_REV, which was WARN-only until 2026-07-24 and
# had been stale at c14b5fc0 since the 2026-07-15 pin to 0a4a554e. Reconciling it
# re-keys compute_recursive_vk_hash(), but nothing external pins that value
# (producer and verifier both recompute it), so it is not a ceremony -- see the
# header of check-p3-rev.sh.
#
# ── ⚑ RECONCILED 2026-08-02 TO fc3c6df: THIS FILE WAS THE STALE ONE. ────────────────────
# P3_REV had read 0a4a554e since 45d1f171c created this file, and was NEVER bumped. On
# 2026-07-30 `d7ba0c4d3` moved the AUTHORITATIVE root-Cargo.toml pin to `rev = "fc3c6df"`
# -- fc3c6dfac26e2082653d2a617a1740446ce33f05, a DESCENDANT of 0a4a554e by exactly two
# commits (4aead01 child-VK-cap targets, then fc3c6df itself). Resolution, not assumption:
# every `plonky3-recursion` entry in Cargo.lock records
#   source = "git+...?rev=fc3c6df#fc3c6dfac26e2082653d2a617a1740446ce33f05"
# so fc3c6df IS what compiles, and 0a4a554e is what five mirrors still advertised.
#
# fc3c6df is a FLAG DAY (Cargo.toml's own note): a constant's VALUE became a PREPROCESSED
# column of `ConstAir`, so every preprocessed commitment moves and every `RecursionVk` /
# derived anchor changes. Advertising 0a4a554e in RECURSION_P3_REV while compiling fc3c6df
# is precisely the "old recursive proofs stay indistinguishable-by-VK-hash from current
# ones" failure that constant exists to prevent -- it was live for three days.
#
# ⚑ Why the gate never said so: the AUTHORITATIVE pin is abbreviated to SEVEN hex chars in
# Cargo.toml, and check-p3-rev.sh matched only `[0-9a-f]{40}`. It therefore extracted NO rev
# from the authoritative source and reported "the authoritative pin has VANISHED (dep
# renamed/removed?)" -- a real, three-day, security-relevant drift misdiagnosed as a missing
# dependency. The gate now accepts a 7--40 hex pin and resolves it through Cargo.lock.
P3_REV=fc3c6dfac26e2082653d2a617a1740446ce33f05
